#: Game/Levels/TutorialWorld/L10rcases1and.lean:14
msgid "# Advanced Tutorial World\n"
"\n"
"## The §0 tactic\n"
"\n"
"Next tactic: §1 (the §2 stands for *recursive*: it can take apart\n"
"nested hypotheses in one go). It does many things, so we'll spend a couple of levels on it.\n"
"It always works on hypotheses and transforms them in different ways. The first\n"
"case is when you have a hypothesis saying that both §3\n"
"and §4 hold, that is, §5. Then §6\n"
"replaces §7 with two new hypotheses, §8 and §9. The angle brackets §10\n"
"(typed §11 and §12) just list the names you want to give to the pieces.\n"
"\n"
"You usually do this for tidiness, since §13 and §14 are also proofs of §15 and §16.\n"
"\n"
"I'm sure you can finish this level on your own. It's only two lines!"
msgstr ""

