#: Game/TacticDoc.lean:23
msgid "## Summary\n"
"\n"
"If §0 is a proof of §1, then §2 swaps\n"
"every §3 in the goal for a §4.\n"
"\n"
"**Variants:** §5 swaps §6 for §7, and\n"
"§8 does the swap in the hypothesis §9 instead\n"
"of in the goal.\n"
"\n"
"## Details\n"
"\n"
"§10 is the 'substitute in' tactic. You can use it in two ways.\n"
"\n"
"1) If §11 is a hypothesis (that is, a proof of §12)\n"
"in your local context (the box in the top right)\n"
"and your goal contains some §13s, then §14\n"
"turns them all into §15s.\n"
"\n"
"2) It also works with theorems that are equalities\n"
"(find them in the menu on the left, under Theorem Statements).\n"
"Many of these theorems need some inputs, and you can\n"
"hand them to §16 right away, just like arguments of a function.\n"
"For example, if §17 needs two points and a proof that\n"
"they're on a line, you can write §18.\n"
"If you leave the arguments out, Lean tries to figure them out\n"
"by itself, which works fine most of the time.\n"
"\n"
"**Heads up:** §19 only works when §20 is a proof of something like §21\n"
"or §22. If §23 is a function or an implication, or if it's the\n"
"statement itself rather than its proof, §24 isn't the tool you want.\n"
"For example, §25 is never correct: §26 is the statement,\n"
"not a proof of it. If §27 is the proof, then §28 works.\n"
"\n"
"**Pro tip:** If §29 and you'd rather turn\n"
"§30s into §31s, use §32 (type the arrow with §33,\n"
"that's a small letter L, not the number 1).\n"
"\n"
"### Example\n"
"If it looks like this in the top right hand box:\n"
"§34\n"
"\n"
"then\n"
"\n"
"§35\n"
"\n"
"will change the goal into §36.\n"
"\n"
"### Example\n"
"You can use §37 to change a hypothesis as well.\n"
"For example, if your local context looks like this:\n"
"§38\n"
"then §39 will turn §40 into §41."
msgstr ""

