#: Game/TacticDoc.lean:122
msgid "## Summary\n"
"\n"
"§0 turns a goal §1 into a hypothesis §2\n"
"and a new goal §3. If §4 and §5 are sets, §6 means \"let §7 be any element of §8\".\n"
"If they're propositions, it means \"assume §9 is true\".\n"
"\n"
"## Details\n"
"\n"
"If your goal is a function or an implication §10, then §11\n"
"will always make progress. §12 turns\n"
"\n"
"§13\n"
"\n"
"into\n"
"\n"
"§14\n"
"\n"
"The opposite of §15 is §16: in the situation\n"
"above, §17 turns the goal back into §18.\n"
"\n"
"**Variant:** You can put several names after §19 instead of calling it many times.\n"
"So §20 does the same as §21.\n"
"\n"
"## Example\n"
"\n"
"If your goal is an implication §22, Lean writes\n"
"it as §23. Then §24 reads as\n"
"\"let §25 be a proof of §26\", or, more casually, \"let's assume\n"
"§27 is true\". The goal becomes §28 and §29\n"
"shows up in your local context."
msgstr ""

