#: Game/TacticDoc.lean:316
msgid "## Summary\n"
"\n"
"§0 works on hypotheses. If §1 or §2, then §3\n"
"removes §4 and replaces it with its *ingredients*:\n"
"§5 and §6, or §7 and §8. It also\n"
"works with §9 and with §10.\n"
"Write §11 to pick your own names §12 and §13\n"
"(type §14 and §15 with §16 and §17).\n"
"\n"
"## Details\n"
"\n"
"How do you prove §18? You prove §19 and you prove §20. So a proof of\n"
"§21 has two ingredients, and §22 pulls them out for you.\n"
"\n"
"For example, if your local context contains\n"
"§23\n"
"\n"
"then after §24 it becomes\n"
"§25\n"
"and §26 is gone.\n"
"\n"
"Likewise, §27 is proved by proving §28 and §29,\n"
"and §30 replaces §31 with\n"
"§32\n"
"\n"
"**A shortcut:** if you don't need to rename anything, you can grab the\n"
"ingredients directly: §33 is the first one and §34 the second.\n"
"So with §35, §36 and §37, and you can use them\n"
"right away, e.g. §38. The same works for §39\n"
"(§40 and §41).\n"
"\n"
"Also note that §42 works with §43 (§44 understands\n"
"§45 and §46), but you can't rewrite with an implication.\n"
"\n"
"§47 works with §48 too, but it's a bit different.\n"
"To prove §49 you give a proof of §50 *or* a proof of §51.\n"
"So if §52, then §53 splits your goal in\n"
"two: one with §54 and the other with §55."
msgstr ""

