#: Game/TacticDoc.lean:231
msgid "## Summary\n"
"§0 creates a new goal of proving §1, and adds §2 to the hypotheses of the goal you were working on.\n"
"\n"
"## Details\n"
"Use §3 when you want a fact (or any term) in your local context under a name, so you can use it later.\n"
"\n"
"## Example (have q := ... or have q : Q := ...)\n"
"If the local context contains\n"
"\n"
"§4\n"
"then §5 adds §6 to your local context, leaving it like this:\n"
"\n"
"§7\n"
"\n"
"Strictly speaking you never need §8, since you could always write §9 instead. But a short name makes life easier.\n"
"\n"
"## Example (have q : Q)\n"
"You can also just say what you want to have, without giving a proof, by leaving out the §10. Then Lean adds it as a new goal, so you'll have one more goal than before.\n"
"\n"
"For example if the local context is\n"
"\n"
"§11\n"
"then after §12 you get a new goal\n"
"\n"
"§13\n"
"and your original goal gets §14 added to its hypotheses."
